  <h2>🚨 Why Your Ice Machine Smells Bad</h2>
  <h3>1. Biofilm &amp; Slime Buildup</h3>
  <p>
    Over time, moisture inside the machine creates a slimy layer of bacteria
    (biofilm). This is one of the most common causes of foul odors.
  </p>
  <h3>2. Mold Growth</h3>
  <p>
    Dark, damp environments are perfect for mold—especially in Florida's
    humidity. Mold inside your machine can create strong, musty smells.
  </p>
  <h3>3. Dirty Water Lines or Filter</h3>
  <p>
    If your water supply isn't clean or your filter is overdue, it can affect
    both smell and taste.
  </p>
  <h3>4. Drain Line Issues</h3>
  <p>
    Clogged or dirty drains can cause stagnant water and odor buildup inside
    the system.
  </p>
